BND-13: apply the Qmax capture limit to custom inlets with a RATING curve

getCustomCapturedFlow() computes the per-inlet limit qMax from the
[INLET_USAGE] Qmax value and applies it to DIVERSION curves, but the RATING
(capture vs depth) branch never uses it. Limit the rating capture to
numInlets * qMax, as the on-grade and on-sag standard inlets do. With no
limit (qMax = BIG) the result is unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-13_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c b/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c
index fa52cb3..42a320d 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c
@@ -1952,6 +1952,7 @@ double getCustomCapturedFlow(TInlet* inlet, double q, double d)
         {
             qCaptured = inlet->numInlets * inlet->clogFactor *
                 table_lookupEx(&Curve[c], d * UCF(LENGTH)) / UCF(FLOW);
+            qCaptured = MIN(qCaptured, inlet->numInlets * qMax);
         }
         qCaptured *= sides;
     }
